1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:05,310
How do you find
the area under a curve?

2
00:00:05,360 --> 00:00:07,330
What's the area under y = x², from 0 to 1?

3
00:00:07,380 --> 00:00:09,500
The top is curved,
so width × height won't work

4
00:00:09,550 --> 00:00:12,070
So let's cover it with rectangular bars

5
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:14,240
The bits sticking out above the curve
make it bigger than the real area

6
00:00:14,290 --> 00:00:21,146
What if we cut the bars thinner?

7
00:00:21,196 --> 00:00:24,116
The extra bits disappear
and it closes in on 0.333…

8
00:00:24,166 --> 00:00:26,886
That's integration!
Adding up super-thin bars

9
00:00:26,936 --> 00:00:30,256
∫ is a stretched-out S for "Sum"
x² dx = height × a super-thin width

10
00:00:30,306 --> 00:00:33,356
But do we really have to
cut and add every time?

11
00:00:34,356 --> 00:00:38,106
NEXT: Differentiate the area
and you get the height?
